# Copy the current machine under a new name through the printer settings window and
# assert that the window says it saved. What the copy is worth is asserted outside
# the window: tools/check deletes the preset this writes, diffs it against its
# parent and resolves its print profiles headlessly.
#
#   cockpit start next-layer --model oracle/models/cube_20.stl \
#       --arg=--preset-dialog --arg=printer
#   cockpit run tools/cockpit/scripts/next-layer-save-as.drive
#
# The name field and the "Supports stealth mode" toggle are at fixed places in the
# 1920x1080 window, read off a capture: field (1250,190), toggle (1509,778). The
# toggle is the edit -- Save is enabled only while a value differs from the preset,
# and a copy that reports "nothing has been changed" is precisely the bug this
# proves gone. The parent has silent_mode false, so the copy must carry true.
assert-text "Printer settings"
shot /tmp/cockpit-saveas-0-window.png
click 1250 190
type "Gate Save As"
click 1509 778
click-text "Save as"
find-text "saved Gate Save As"
shot /tmp/cockpit-saveas-1-saved.png
